  "question": {
    "text": "In the circuit shown, current measured by ammeter is <math><mi>x</mi></math> ampere. Find <math><mi>x</mi></math>.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0002_797f9fb782ae.jpg\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 154px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "03.00",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let current = <math><mi>x</mi></math> ampere<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> &amp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> out of phase)<br />Voltage across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi></math><br /><br />Using phase addition of voltage,<br /><math><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi><msup><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>40</mn><msup><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>50</mn><msup><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>"
  }
